Hi Amber,

Sorry for the delay. Looking at the referenced Rmd file, I don't know if there is something fancy going on with that dplyr code that I can't immediately see, but at least in your script I can see that there are a bunch of missing pieces. Here's one method that should work:
In your working projection, you need to calculate the error ellipse covariance matrices, which have the unique components "COV.x.x","COV.x.y","COV.y.y" in ctmm name format. You need all three of these values for every location estimate to make an error ellipse.
After you have imported your data into ctmm and it's in the same projection, then you make the data appear calibrated with uere(DATA) <- 1 though the error information will be bogus thus far.
Then you can copy over the  "COV.x.x","COV.x.y","COV.y.y" columns.
Then there's one final column that you may or may not need, which is the approximate error radius: DATA$VAR.xy <- (DATA$COV.x.x+DATA$COV.y.y)/2
That should leave you with a dataset that registers as calibrated with the correct error ellipse and radius information.

Best,
Chris

